# Git workflow

Follow `CONTRIBUTING.md` for every branch, commit, push, and merge.

- `main` is the newest runnable app: showcase and hosting. Never commit, push, or force-push directly to `main`. Never merge work that does not run.
- Branch from an updated `main`. One branch, one change. Name it `feature/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, or `docs/` plus a lowercase kebab-case description (`feature/split-expenses`).
- Push the same day the branch is created, and after every working commit. Open a draft pull request early so the timeline is visible and two people do not build the same change.
- Update the branch from `main` before the pull request is ready. Merge only through that pull request, then delete the branch.
- Do not commit secrets. `server/.env` stays local.

When asked to commit, push, or open a pull request, use the current task branch. If the work is on `main`, stop and create the branch above first. Do not push to `main` to "update the demo"; the merged pull request is what updates `main`.
